    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9d5ba28b4a920b344a539aa023a70b5f31e4ff1ab408b36d4313cd90a0b64d33",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source distinguishes four maps of zero spacing rather than one interchangeable notion: normalized pair correlation describes a two-point distribution without selecting consecutive pairs; r_n followed by limsup or liminf isolates opposite extremes of consecutive all-zero gaps while discarding their frequency; Λ changes the underlying sequence to consecutive critical-line zeros; and the cited global-versus-local averaging method gives a frequency-bearing inequality for fixed-r gaps. Their comparison therefore separates distributional, extremal, population-restricted, and multi-step frequency questions.",
